/* ── Signature [scope-140] ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* nostromo's approved signature (Kenny, 2026-10-03, three review rounds): the
   progress bar and the ten elements (spinner, skeleton, switch, check and
   radio, toast, dialog, tooltip, wizard steps, empty state, link hover),
   ported once from research/progress-signature/themes/nostromo.css and research/signature-elements/themes/nostromo.css
   and maintained here from now on. In kp.signature, which css/themes.css
   orders after kp.register, so it draws over the register exactly as the
   approved demos did, whatever the weight of a register selector. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The dashboard parts: action tiles, status rows, the facet list, the heat grid, the matrix, the bar in a cell, the
   week agenda and the run timeline [kpadopt2] ──
   Nostromo's own (themes/nostromo/CHARACTER.md): a tile is a switch on the console, raised beige moulding with its
   lamp before the title (G6, G7, G8): unlit at rest, lit under the hand, full when pressed, the LED with its glow on
   keyboard focus; a press pushes the key into a well and nothing moves (G14); a warning sounds the klaxon, the carrier
   framed all round in the tone (G13); label tape names, Michroma counts (G15); waiting is the lamp bank computing, the
   LED window's unordered patterns on the frame clock (G10): a heat grid's row of cells is one LED window, a count one
   short window, never a clipped word in every cell; a running run is that window lit along it. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The dashboard parts: what the package leaves to a register [kpadopt2-repairs] ──
   Formal keeps these parts exactly as Kenny approved them; this theme takes the three repairs the review asks for: a
   loading heat grid or matrix row as tall as its ready row (no skeleton gap between cells), an empty or failed run
   timeline with a lane-sized space for its sentence (never over the legend), the sentence as wide as its words on the
   theme's ground (never through a rule or a ghost bar), and an axis label near the end edge standing before its rule. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The six opt-in options of the dashboard adoption, round 3, in this theme [kpadopt3] ──
   The nav bar's separator, the timeline's day buttons and series runs, the week agenda's upcoming list on a phone and
   the facet swatch's identity pattern (the choice-filter value and the heat grid's End are behaviour only).
   Nostromo's own (themes/nostromo/CHARACTER.md): the separator is a panel seam, a dark joint with its
   light lip and one unlit lamp at its middle; lying down across the phone's list it is the same seam. A day on the axis
   lights its rim in the LED orange under the pointer; pressed it is a key sunk in its well, its lamp lit under the
   date. The upcoming list names today in the LED orange; the facet pattern is a key in its well. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in nostromo's grammar: data pieces, empty-state drawings [kpadopt4] ──
   Nostromo's own (themes/nostromo/CHARACTER.md): the case is what you touch and the screen is what the ship reports
   (G7). A mark is a label plate (tape, 2 px, G6) with a lamp-lit pattern when it is a picture; a share bar is a lit
   window, its parts lit lenses and the free rest the unlit cells (G10's window); labels are tape, counts Michroma
   (G15); a changed reading lights its lamp (G9); a failed carrier sounds the klaxon (G13); a block of code or a command
   is a screen: amber phosphor on dark glass under scanlines, set in the plate's bezel (G7). Every drawing in an empty
   state is a vector written on such a screen, the raster's order, frame by frame (G2, G4). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in nostromo's grammar: rows, tiles, check lists, card states [kpadopt4] ──
   A row of a list is a line on the console's log: its state is a lit bar along the start edge, and a row that warns or
   fails sounds the klaxon, framed all round, 3 px, in the tone (G13); a payload a row folds away is the ship's printout
   on its small screen (G7). A tile of choices is a moulded key: raised at rest, lit rim under the hand, sunk in its well
   when it is ticked (G8, G14); its title is label tape. A fix written out for a check is a readout on a screen. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in nostromo's grammar: pipeline, journey, moments, secret, dialog sections [kpadopt4] ──
   The pipeline is a rack: a lane a moulded plate, its head label tape with the stage's lit strip, a card a key with its
   lamp (G8): unlit at rest, lit under the hand, full when pressed, the LED orange on the open one; the board's words
   are a plate, a failed read the klaxon (G13). A journey is the LED bargraph laid between its steps: the way travelled
   lit in the step's own colour, the way to come unlit cells, a failed way alternate cells in red; the step it stands at
   is a lamp lit in its key. A moment on the timeline is a lamp, a stretch a run of lit cells (G10's window). The secret
   field is a screen: the value is written on it by the raster (G2) and the countdown is a bargraph that goes out cell by
   cell (G9, G10); a dialog's sections are divided by the vent seam and its danger section is framed all round (G13). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in nostromo's grammar: time, cooking and comparison [kpadopt4] ──
   Everything that reads a time out is the ship's screen: the digits of a countdown, a timer's remaining time and the
   timer disc are amber phosphor on dark glass in the case's bezel (G7, G15); an ended timer sounds the klaxon, framed
   all round and never flashing (G13); the uptime strip is a lit window whose cells light by state (G10's window); the
   wheel turns in whole frames of the ship's clock and its outcome is written on the screen (G1, G4); a three-way chip
   is a switch with its lamp, lit in ink, in red for out (G8, G13); the quantity's figure is Michroma in its well and
   its unit label tape (G15); a checklist is the log with its dotted seams; cook mode's ingredients are a printout. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── kpadopt4 repairs found at 390 px [kpadopt4] ──
   A label set in this theme's wide letters needs more room than the aside leaves it in a narrow form: below 36rem of the
   form's own width each row is its own column (label, control, then the aside under it), so no label ever runs into the aside. The countdown's
   colon takes the room of a monospaced character. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── A sort the page carries out [kpadopt4]: the sorted header has its lamp lit (G8, G9) ──
   Every sortable header keeps an unlit lamp before its name (25 %), so the header never changes width when it is the
   sorted one; the sorted header's lamp is the LED, lit, and the arrow after the name keeps the direction. A column that
   cannot be sorted now has no lamp and no arrow. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* A destructive button that stands on a destructive plate (the urgent and the refused question card, a failed plate with its
   action) is drawn like the card's other button: a destructive fill on a destructive plate, or red ink on orange, left it
   without a plate [t56-eye-1018]. */
@layer kp.signature {

